# rop_image

- Label: ROP Image Output
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 1
- Parameters: 76 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: yes

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/rop_image.html
- Summary (EN): The ROP Image Copernicus node writes the output of a COP network to disk as image files. It is the Image ROP placed inside a COP network and renders the COP chosen by its COP Path parameter.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud ROP Image écrit sur disque, sous forme de fichiers image, la sortie d'un réseau COP, en rendant le COP désigné par son chemin.

- Inputs meaning: ["The page lists no numbered inputs; a wired input is used only by the Add AOVs from Input button, which imports AOVs from its outputs", "Otherwise the source to render is set by the COP Path parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Render to Disk / Render to MPlay / Render to Disk in Background: where the images go", "Valid Frame Range: current frame, a range that can include referenced frames, or a strict Start/End/Inc range", "UDIM List: Disabled, Use Context, Explicit or Range", "COP Path: the COP node or subnetwork to render", "Output File: file path with tokens LAYER (one file per AOV), F / F# (frame number) and UDIM", "Colorspace Conversion: OpenColorIO Colorspace, Bake to OpenColorIO Display/View, or Raw", "Set Default Resolution / Pixel Scale / Border / Precision: each overrides the COP node value when enabled", "File Layout (AOV list): name, data size, Raw toggle and optional explicit Port index per AOV", "Save Retries: retries of a save that fails due to a disk or network error"]

- Caveats: ["AOVs added out of sequential order need explicit Port parameters to get the correct order", "The Default Resolution override does not apply when the resolution comes from a File COP or a SOP-converted volume; the page suggests a Resample COP to force a resolution", "Save in Background can speed up large files but uses more memory, since it keeps the output until the save finishes"]

